      "text": "We want to maximize the quadratic:\n\n\\[\n-4z^2 + 20z - 6\n\\]\n\nSince the coefficient of \\(z^2\\) is negative, the parabola opens downward, so the maximum occurs at the vertex.\n\nFor a quadratic \\(az^2 + bz + c\\), the vertex is at:\n\n\\[\nz = -\\frac{b}{2a}\n\\]\n\nHere, \\(a = -4\\), \\(b = 20\\):\n\n\\[\nz = -\\frac{20}{2(-4)} = -\\frac{20}{-8} = \\frac{5}{2}\n\\]\n\nNow plug \\(z = \\frac{5}{2}\\) into the expression:\n\n\\[\n-4\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)^2 + 20\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right) - 6\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= -4 \\cdot \\frac{25}{4} + 50 - 6\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= -25 + 50 - 6 = 19\n\\]\n\nThe maximum value is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{19}\n\\]\n\nThe answer is 19.",
