    {
      "text": "The quadratic has a negative leading coefficient, so its maximum occurs at the vertex.  \n\nFor \\(-4z^2+20z-6\\), the vertex is at  \n\\[\nz=-\\frac{20}{2(-4)}=\\frac52.\n\\]\nSubstituting:\n\\[\n-4\\left(\\frac52\\right)^2+20\\left(\\frac52\\right)-6\n=-25+50-6=19.\n\\]\n\nThe answer is 19.",
